dsh-tool-guardian README · Configure：Tool Guardian reads the **standard** `mcpServers` block (the same shape Claude Desktop / Claude Code and most MCP clients use):

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "files": {
      "command": "npx",

An optional per-server `"description"` enriches the catalogue the model sees. Without one, the hint is derived from that server's own tool names at startup.

dsh-tool-guardian README · Environment and `.env`："env": {"GITHUB_TOKEN": "${GITHUB_TOKEN}"}

(Up to 0.7.0 only `args` were expanded, so an `env` value like that reached
  the server as the literal text `${GITHUB_TOKEN}`.)

dsh-tool-guardian README · Remote servers：A `"url"` entry is a remote MCP server over Streamable HTTP, routed like any stdio server:

```json
{"mcpServers": {
  "docs": {"url": "https://mcp.example.org/mcp", "headers": {"Authorization": "Bearer ${MY_TOKEN}"}},
  "local": {"url": "http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp"}
}}

dsh-tool-guardian README · Remote servers：**Not done:** OAuth (wrap the server in `mcp-remote` as in the `args` example under "Variable expansion"; it
does the sign-in and the router sees a plain stdio command); resuming a dropped stream (`Last-Event-ID`) and the standalone `GET` stream of Streamable HTTP;
`subscriptions/listen`; and server requests for input (elicitation).

